Android FFmpeg/ffprobe and codec libraries come from the official Termux package
repository. Package versions and original archive SHA-256 values are recorded in
android/native/ffmpeg-aarch64.json, copied to the payload as ffmpeg-packages.json.

Upstream source: https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/tree/n9.0.2
Android build recipes and patches: https://github.com/termux/termux-packages/tree/master/packages/ffmpeg

The APK renames versioned library filenames and their ELF SONAME/DT_NEEDED strings,
and replaces the Termux RUNPATH with $ORIGIN. These packaging transformations are
implemented in scripts/android-native.ts and build-ffmpeg-android-native.ts.
FFmpeg is invoked as a separate executable process by the Bun backend.
